   "source": [
    "# ⚛️ Fine-Tuning Meta Llama-3.1-8B as an AI Quantum Algorithm Tutor\n",
    "### **Project: Quantum Leap (Smart India Hackathon 2026 — Problem 4)**\n",
    "\n",
    "[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/saketsumanai/Quantum-Project/blob/main/notebooks/Quantum_Llama_Tutor_Colab_FineTuning.ipynb)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a complete, production-grade pipeline to fine-tune **Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct** using **QLoRA (4-bit quantization)** on a **free Google Colab T4 GPU** (or A100/L4).\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **What this model learns:**\n",
    "1. **Socratic Pedagogy**: Explaining complex quantum principles (superposition, entanglement, phase kickback) using intuitive everyday analogies.\n",
    "2. **Rigorous Mathematics**: Producing clean, exact LaTeX Dirac notation and operator matrices.\n",
    "3. **Runnable Code**: Generating verified, production-grade Qiskit 1.0+ circuits with no deprecated syntax.\n",
    "4. **Active Misconception Diagnosis**: Formulating diagnostic quizzes with realistic distractors and clear diagnostic feedback.\n",
    "5. **Textbook Grounding**: Accurate academic citations from canonical texts (Nielsen & Chuang, Watrous, Preskill)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Check GPU Acceleration\n",
    "Make sure your Colab runtime is set to **T4 GPU**:\n",
    "`Runtime` -> `Change runtime type` -> Select **T4 GPU**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!nvidia-smi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Install High-Performance Training Dependencies\n",
    "We use **Unsloth / Hugging Face TRL & PEFT** for 2x-5x faster training with minimal VRAM overhead."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q --upgrade pip\n",
    "!pip install -q torch transformers datasets peft bitsandbytes trl accelerate qiskit\n",
    "print(\"✅ Dependencies successfully installed!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Load the Socratic Quantum Training Dataset\n",
    "We load the curated dataset containing canonical quantum topics: Bell States, Grover's Search, Shor's Algorithm, QFT, VQE, and Error Correction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from datasets import Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "# You can upload your quantum_tutor_dataset.jsonl directly or use the built-in generator\n",
    "dataset_url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/saketsumanai/Quantum-Project/main/data/quantum_tutor_dataset.jsonl\"\n",
    "\n",
    "import urllib.request\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    urllib.request.urlretrieve(dataset_url, \"quantum_tutor_dataset.jsonl\")\n",
    "    print(\"Downloaded latest dataset from repository!\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Using local upload: {e}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(\"quantum_tutor_dataset.jsonl\", \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    records = [json.loads(line) for line in f if line.strip()]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_data = Dataset.from_list(records)\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(train_data)} high-quality quantum training samples.\")\n",
    "print(\"Sample instruction:\", train_data[0]['instruction'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Configure 4-bit Quantization (QLoRA) and Load Llama-3.1-8B\n",
    "BitsAndBytes NF4 quantization reduces model memory from 16GB to ~5.5GB VRAM, leaving plenty of room for batch processing on a free T4 GPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer, BitsAndBytesConfig\n",
    "from peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model, prepare_model_for_kbit_training\n",
    "\n",
    "model_id = \"meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Note: Provide your Hugging Face access token with Llama-3.1 access\n",
    "# from huggingface_hub import login\n",
    "# login()\n",
    "\n",
    "bnb_config = BitsAndBytesConfig(\n",
    "    load_in_4bit=True,\n",
    "    bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\",\n",
    "    bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.bfloat16 if torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported() else torch.float16,\n",
    "    bnb_4bit_use_double_quant=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_id, trust_remote_code=True)\n",
    "if tokenizer.pad_token is None:\n",
    "    tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n",
    "tokenizer.padding_side = \"right\"\n",
    "\n",
    "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    model_id,\n",
    "    quantization_config=bnb_config,\n",
    "    device_map=\"auto\",\n",
    "    trust_remote_code=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "model = prepare_model_for_kbit_training(model)\n",
    "\n",
    "peft_config = LoraConfig(\n",
    "    r=16,\n",
    "    lora_alpha=32,\n",
    "    lora_dropout=0.05,\n",
    "    bias=\"none\",\n",
    "    task_type=\"CAUSAL_LM\",\n",
    "    target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"o_proj\", \"gate_proj\", \"up_proj\", \"down_proj\"],\n",
    ")\n",
    "model = get_peft_model(model, peft_config)\n",
    "model.print_trainable_parameters()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Format Chat Template and Train with SFTTrainer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from trl import SFTTrainer\n",
    "from transformers import TrainingArguments\n",
    "\n",
    "def format_prompts(example):\n",
    "    return {\"text\": tokenizer.apply_chat_template(example[\"messages\"], tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=False)}\n",
    "\n",
    "formatted_dataset = train_data.map(format_prompts)\n",
    "\n",
    "training_args = TrainingArguments(\n",
    "    output_dir=\"./quantum_llama_tutor_lora\",\n",
    "    num_train_epochs=3,\n",
    "    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n",
    "    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n",
    "    learning_rate=2e-4,\n",
    "    lr_scheduler_type=\"cosine\",\n",
    "    warmup_ratio=0.05,\n",
    "    logging_steps=1,\n",
    "    save_strategy=\"epoch\",\n",
    "    fp16=not torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",
    "    bf16=torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",
    "    report_to=\"none\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "trainer = SFTTrainer(\n",
    "    model=model,\n",
    "    train_dataset=formatted_dataset,\n",
    "    dataset_text_field=\"text\",\n",
    "    max_seq_length=2048,\n",
    "    tokenizer=tokenizer,\n",
    "    args=training_args,\n",
    "    peft_config=peft_config,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🚀 Starting QLoRA Training on GPU...\")\n",
    "trainer.train()\n",
    "print(\"✨ Training successfully completed!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Test Inference & Verify Socratic Quantum Output\n",
    "Test the fine-tuned model with a query about Grover's search."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "eval_prompt = [\n",
    "    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are Aura Quantum AI. Output valid JSON.\"\},\n",
    "    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Explain how the Grover diffusion operator amplifies target probabilities in quantum search.\"}\n",
    "]\n",
    "input_text = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(eval_prompt, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n",
    "inputs = tokenizer(input_text, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(\"cuda\")\n",
    "\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    outputs = model.generate(\n",
    "        **inputs,\n",
    "        max_new_tokens=800,\n",
    "        temperature=0.2,\n",
    "        do_sample=True,\n",
    "        pad_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "response_text = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0][inputs['input_ids'].shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- MODEL RESPONSE ---\\n\")\n",
    "print(response_text)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Save & Export Adapters for Ollama or Hugging Face Hub\n",
    "Run this cell to save the trained adapter or push to your Hugging Face repository."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save locally\n",
    "output_dir = \"./quantum_llama_tutor_lora\"\n",
    "trainer.model.save_pretrained(output_dir)\n",
    "tokenizer.save_pretrained(output_dir)\n",
    "print(f\"Saved LoRA adapter to {output_dir}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optional: push to HuggingFace Hub\n",
    "# trainer.model.push_to_hub(\"your-hf-username/quantum-llama-3.1-8b-tutor\")\n",
    "# tokenizer.push_to_hub(\"your-hf-username/quantum-llama-3.1-8b-tutor\")"
   ]
  }
